\title{Addendum: Mordell--Weil Data for the Fibration\\
$E_{n}\colon Y^{2}=X^{3}+36n^{2}X^{2}+12ncX+c^{2}$, $c=36n^{3}-19$}
\author{}
\date{}

\begin{document}
\maketitle

The Diophantine equation $y^{2}=(36n^{3}-19-12mn)^{2}-(2m)^{3}$ is, for fixed
$n$ and under $X=-2m$, $Y=y$, the elliptic fibration above. Integer solutions
with parameter $n$ correspond to integral points on $E_{n}$ with $X$ even;
the trivial family $m=0$ corresponds to the tautological section
$T=(0,\,c)$.

\begin{proposition}[Tautological torsion section]
The section $T=(0,c)$ satisfies $2T=(0,-c)$ and $3T=O$ on every fiber: it is
a section of exact order $3$. \textup{(}Verified numerically via canonical
heights and \texttt{ellorder} on fibers across the table; algebraically,
$x(2T)=\bigl(\tfrac{a_4}{2c}\bigr)^{2}-a_2-\dots=0$ reduces to the identity
$(12nc)^{2}=4c^{2}\cdot 36n^{2}$.\textup{)} Consequently the generic rank of
the family receives no contribution from $T$, and
$\mathbb{Z}/3\mathbb{Z}\subseteq E_{n}(\mathbb{Q})_{\mathrm{tors}}$ for all $n$.
\end{proposition}

